\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/block.fam — a block: parsing it, and verifying its proof (see
\ ../rust/src/block.rs, prover.rs `verify_tree`, aggregate.rs `verify_block`).
\
\ Header (188 bytes; integers big-endian): version (4), prev_hash, state_root,
\ body_hash, aux_hash (32 each), output_count, height, timestamp (8 each),
\ nonce (32).  Body: inputs, outputs (a 4-byte big-endian count, then 32
\ bytes each), nonces (count, 16 bytes each), the block proof and the parent's
\ chain proof (a 4-byte big-endian length, then the bytes).
\
\ The block proof is a tree root: kind 1, its amounts A and B (8 bytes each,
\ little-endian), whether it aggregates (1) or wraps one chunk (0), its data
\ (32 bytes), then the root's STARK proof.  It's verified as a circuit-VM
\ proof whose public bus tuples are the tree node's eight public octets:
\   [vk, data, amounts, root_in, root_out, counts, challenge, product]
\ -- vk the aggregation key's digest (zeros for a wrap); counts the output
\ counts in and out and the block's window, as 20-bit limb pairs; challenge
\ a hash of data and the body; product the body's commitments' product.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

\ ── The network's tree keys and parameters ──

: bnet variable ;   \ 0: main, 1: dev

